#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 900.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120576} :activity/id #uuid "ed79a46b-23ff-5442-970b-42e684476845" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051045 :topic/id #uuid "7cf45c34-fae0-53a3-89c2-bd091d1c7405" :topic/math-academy-id 1838} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120576 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186121001 :tutorial/content "Consider the curve $C$ parametrized by the vector function \n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle 2\\sin t, \\: 2\\cos t, \\: \\sqrt{5} t\\rangle, \\qquad t \\ge 0.\n$$\n\n \n\nFor any $t >0,$ the arc length $s$ of $C$ from $\\mathbf r(0)$ to $\\mathbf r(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,du \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,\\sqrt{5}⟩‖\\,du \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\sqrt{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)^{2}+(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u)^{2}+(\\sqrt{5})^{2}}\\,du \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\sqrt{4({cos}^{2}⁡u+{sin}^{2}⁡u)+5}\\,du \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\sqrt{9}\\,du \\\\  & =3u{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =3t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $s= 3t,$ or equivalently $t = \\dfrac{s}{3}.$ \n\nNow, we can define a new vector function $\\mathbf{R}$ as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf R(s)= \\mathbf r\\left(\\dfrac{s}{3}\\right) = \\left\\langle 2\\sin \\left(\\dfrac{s}{3}\\right), \\: 2\\cos \\left(\\dfrac{s}{3}\\right), \\: \\sqrt{5} \\left(\\dfrac{s}{3}\\right) \\right\\rangle .\n$$\n\nThe function $\\mathbf{R}(s)$ gives us the *same* curve $C,$ but this time it is parameterized by the arc length $s.$\n\nIn general, if $\\mathbf r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b]$ is a continuously differentiable vector function such that $\\mathbf r'(t )\\neq \\mathbf{0},$ then to parametrize it in terms of arc length we perform the following steps:\n\n1\\. Compute $s = \\displaystyle s(t) = \\int_a^t\\|\\mathbf r'(u)\\| \\, \\mathrm{d}u$\n\n2\\. Write $s = s(t)$ in the form $t=t(s)$\n\n3\\. Substitute $t=t(s)$ back into $\\mathbf r(t)$ to get $\\mathbf R(s)=\\mathbf r(t(s))$\n\n**Note:** One advantage of parametrizing a curve by its arc length is that the tangent vector is always a unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\left\\|\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}\\mathbf R}{\\textrm{d} s}\\right\\| = 1\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "a2ecbf26-2299-5d4f-9ca0-ac626810c1ee" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2375 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "3cac974a-1992-543d-93ed-f87c6e569e32" :step/math-academy-id 10294 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120577}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120577 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119745 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119561 :question/id #uuid "9b2026e3-781b-5e73-8dc2-0e8f2789fe67" :question/math-academy-id "e-3065"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2c4b9b-cf73-56d1-96b1-73f48b50ed7b" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049317}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120279} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120286} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262811} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314853} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319302} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387824} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443543} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443544} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443548}] :knowledge-point/title "Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length Given Its Arc Length"} :step/id #uuid "316716f0-90d4-5cb3-8194-1e5c03222fc9" :step/math-academy-id 10295 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120579}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120578 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119746 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119562 :question/id #uuid "74f33486-6391-5ec0-8a5b-bb51c9af2d55" :question/math-academy-id "e-3066"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aecbb8b-bda3-5956-9b0f-98509330a84d" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048418}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120287} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120288} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262816} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262817} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262818} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262819} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348078} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387838} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393842} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443547} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443549}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"} :step/id #uuid "d0612bf4-b80b-510a-873d-f90bcf69f311" :step/math-academy-id 10298} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120579 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119747 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119563 :question/id #uuid "48350682-3ad0-5311-bb47-782ec454390c" :question/math-academy-id "e-3067"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc7343e3-fa7d-58c8-b4c7-49ef5b85110b" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048999}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120280} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120356} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262814} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262815} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314864} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348079} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387831} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393835} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393849} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443542} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443545} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443546} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485503} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485542}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Tangent Given the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"} :step/id #uuid "beb05cc6-e9de-51c2-91d9-49857b9e53c6" :step/math-academy-id 10301 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120578}}] :activity/title "Parameterization by Arc Length" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186120037}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485597} :activity/id #uuid "18d7af17-233d-5b5e-b9c1-9d6300fdb16f" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051045 :topic/id #uuid "7cf45c34-fae0-53a3-89c2-bd091d1c7405" :topic/math-academy-id 1838} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485597 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120356 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "808c3d96-e051-54b7-abc8-f503d0f4399f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,i-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,j-\\frac{1}{2}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485095} {:answer/id #uuid "8516513a-8c46-5d5b-9c96-4f7574d94c8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,j+\\frac{1}{2}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485105} {:answer/id #uuid "c575acd8-bd34-5084-ac96-b6d573032127" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{s}{2}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{2}\\,j-\\frac{s}{2}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485240} {:answer/id #uuid "cbc40c26-154e-540c-b167-bab2ca6ddfbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,j-\\frac{1}{2}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485252} {:answer/id #uuid "e226f754-b94d-52bf-a072-a6d3d6155d75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "T(s)=\\,i+\\sqrt{3}\\,j-\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485295}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485252} :answer-field/id #uuid "b10f0145-3d4d-5529-9dac-9ea4a90d8cc8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118250}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dcc2eb2b-f195-52bb-b223-b20a6a536e9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-34666" :question/problem "Given the curve  $r(t)=(t+2)\\,i+(\\sqrt{2}t-2)\\,j-t\\,k,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=2t$, find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=2t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{s}{2}+2)i+(\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{s}{2}-2)j-\\frac{s}{2}\\,k \\\\  & =(\\frac{s+4}{2})i+(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s-4}{2})j-\\frac{s}{2}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s+4}{2})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s-4}{2})j-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{2})k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}i+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,j-\\frac{1}{2}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "05097e08-aba7-5438-8b05-16aa93723026" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485620}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485615 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485503 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00d50bca-92fb-55a8-95fa-679d33e3532a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484814} {:answer/id #uuid "48d183bf-007f-5b04-a232-41002099c1e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "T(s)=⟨\\sqrt{5},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484975} {:answer/id #uuid "714608fd-7b16-5349-b7e9-a6f3edf1f4dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "T(s)=⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3},\\,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485061} {:answer/id #uuid "9bc2226e-ee70-510d-bc66-ff349daea915" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\sqrt{5},\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485156} {:answer/id #uuid "b21b8788-0001-5c14-9230-a8c727b9b478" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{1}{4}⟨\\sqrt{7},\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485203}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485156} :answer-field/id #uuid "589092fa-ff4f-5507-8f77-fd531d740c3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485402}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1bd4e151-d470-5686-8d26-76a2f90fc9ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-127705" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨t\\sqrt{5},\\,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=3t,$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=3t,$ we have that $t=\\frac{s}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{3}) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{s\\sqrt{5}}{3},\\,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parameterized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s\\sqrt{5}}{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\sqrt{5},\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "3bcda2f1-0662-50da-b09c-0d28fb5181b7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485639}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485617 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485542 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "320f4aa0-708b-5ab1-987b-059bdbf94bf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{3}}⟨\\sqrt{3+s},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\,-\\sqrt{3-s}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484922} {:answer/id #uuid "552a44df-a03e-5e37-b037-66869b26d4bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\sqrt{1+s},\\,\\sqrt{2},\\,-\\sqrt{1-s}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485008} {:answer/id #uuid "84627639-2fe8-58d5-8d64-3bfd4d45a9b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\sqrt{1+3s},\\,\\sqrt{2},\\,-\\sqrt{1-3s}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485102} {:answer/id #uuid "bb9fb01c-a4f1-5042-9365-5d57dca9b009" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\sqrt{1+3s},\\,\\sqrt{6},\\,-\\sqrt{1-3s}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485219} {:answer/id #uuid "f6f69e6c-4bfb-5375-8773-8a19353ec55e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\sqrt{3+s},\\,\\sqrt{3},\\,-\\sqrt{3-s}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485346}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484922} :answer-field/id #uuid "72fd9bc1-8b09-5167-a079-9e30ee96793c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485414}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "72798764-caa8-5165-8cde-e9f5d6b201ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-129738" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨\\frac{4}{3}(1+t)^{3/2},\\,t,\\,\\frac{4}{3}(1-t)^{3/2}⟩,$ $-1\\le t\\le 1,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=3t,$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=3t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{3}) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{4}{3}{(1+\\frac{s}{3})}^{3/2},\\,\\frac{s}{3},\\,\\frac{4}{3}{(1-\\frac{s}{3})}^{3/2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parameterized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4}{3}{(1+\\frac{s}{3})}^{3/2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4}{3}{(1+\\frac{s}{3})}^{3/2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{s}{3}},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,-\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{1-\\frac{s}{3}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{3}}⟨\\sqrt{3+s},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\,-\\sqrt{3-s}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "4bd8b9d3-7cea-57a9-9675-f5a41a91f0b7"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485620 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393842 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fc4c695-abde-5448-ab84-839794d4b9a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(s)\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(s)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393844} {:answer/id #uuid "82715f51-4266-5316-ba54-15a96b26aea9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{cos}^{4}⁡(s)\\,i+{sin}^{4}⁡(s)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393845} {:answer/id #uuid "986a4e80-ffd7-5103-99bd-9d5fbf8fa7ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡({s}^{4})\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡({s}^{4})\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393846} {:answer/id #uuid "7aeedef8-6d70-5a50-8672-9a39d5a5f8be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(s)\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(s)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393847} {:answer/id #uuid "12c6fdf5-7cf6-53c1-8053-8f7bd4a787ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡({s}^{3})\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({s}^{3})\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393848}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393847} :answer-field/id #uuid "96e7a5ea-46f6-52ca-814b-b0356c2e00b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d899d29b-8ceb-54bb-99b6-823abccec15f" :question/math-academy-id "q-78391" :question/problem "What is the parametrization of the curve $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{4})\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{4})\\,j,$  $\\,t\\ge 0,$ by its arc length $s?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{4}))i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{4}))j \\\\  & =-4{t}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{4})\\,i+4{t}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{4})\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{[-4{t}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{4})]}^{2}+{[4{t}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{4})]}^{2}} \\\\  & =4|t{|}^{3}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡({t}^{4})+{cos}^{2}⁡({t}^{4})} \\\\  & =4{t}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}4{u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={u}^{4}\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & ={t}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNow, since $s={t}^{4}$, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{4} & =s \\\\ t & =\\sqrt[4]{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\sqrt[4]{s}) \\\\  & =cos\\,((\\sqrt[4]{s})^{4})\\,i+sin\\,((\\sqrt[4]{s})^{4})\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(s)\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(s)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "62a95bfa-418a-54b0-9d24-b05b00712567" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485615}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485639 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262817 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "024627dc-383d-5860-af06-8aa6e2da6ab6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{3}})-2,\\,1-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{3}})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259889} {:answer/id #uuid "373cd070-c493-5aea-bf0e-9215551aac13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3s-2,\\,1-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260368} {:answer/id #uuid "9e6395f8-6ebe-5c9f-b14e-154974e4a4ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261248} {:answer/id #uuid "e4ce8f43-76db-5d23-b911-0dec03f55f84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "R(s)=-3⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261887} {:answer/id #uuid "fab3aaa0-4b41-5a1b-9408-231dbe0c5b7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})-2,\\,1-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262067}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262067} :answer-field/id #uuid "db150d83-e01a-590a-b532-af881f45cce8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262504}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "40071fab-d489-5d46-9356-22b420cd3a67" :question/math-academy-id "q-127732" :question/problem "What is the parametrization of the curve $r(t)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2,\\,1-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ by its arc length $s?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+{(-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+9{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3u\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =3t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $s=3t,$ we have that $t=\\frac{s}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{3}) \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})-2,\\,1-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "d577c1cf-a49a-5811-96be-ab42adc328f1" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485617}}] :activity/title "Parameterization by Arc Length" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484805}]}
